 forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Nellie Pou (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Nellie Pou seeks re-election in a North Jersey district that Donald Trump carried, making it one of the few Trump-won seats Democrats are defending. Her Republican challenger, Rosie Pino, won the primary in June but has struggled financially, with about $13,000 on hand compared to Pou's $1.08 million. The Bergen Record has endorsed Pou, and Politico reports that deportation politics are complicating the GOP's pitch to Hispanic voters in the district.\n\nEvery major rating outlet, from Cook and Inside Elections to the Economist and Split Ticket, places the race at Safe or Solid Democratic, with a few at Likely Democratic. Kalshi and Polymarket both price Pou's chances at roughly 97 percent. With no public polling available, the forecast rests on fundamentals, ratings, and markets, all of which point to a comfortable Pou win in the mid-teens.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.969, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9625, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9596, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9671, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9566, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9555, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9611, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9621, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9669, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9744, "margin": 13.4}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.969, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9657, "margin": 12.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9546, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9588, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9626, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9636, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9617, "margin": 12.5}, 